Rustarche
A Rust skill for Claude Code. Also serves as a language skill for metarche (https://github.com/metapbl/Metarche).

Basis: the research report "Rust guidelines by expert consensus" (2026-11-13, kept by the author) and six research notes.
Only the approaches and facts of the sources the report cites were used. No text was copied.

- Rust official: API Guidelines, Edition Guide, Cargo Book (Build performance, config, workspaces, rust-version),
  Clippy Book (Usage, lints), RELEASES.md, Nomicon
- Microsoft Pragmatic Rust Guidelines — https://microsoft.github.io/rust-guidelines/
- Effective Rust (David Drysdale), Rust Design Patterns, The Rust Performance Book (Nicholas Nethercote)
- BurntSushi "Using unwrap() in Rust is Okay", Luca Palmieri "Error Handling in Rust",
  matklad (How to Test, Large Rust Workspaces), Alice Ryhl (blocking, actors), the Tokio documentation
- Kent Beck "Augmented Coding", the fish shell port
- Agent guideline files of ruff and uv (Astral), zed, codex
- Anthropic Claude Code documentation (Best practices, Memory, Hooks)
- RustEvo² (arXiv:2503.16922)

Checked against: Rust 1.100.0 (2026-11), Windows MSVC toolchain.
